{"content":"---\nname: project-shadow-frontier\ndescription: \"Shadow Frontier: successor project to the defect-cocycle program — S-unit rigidity, band-crossing certificates, high-complexity trap search\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 3d506146-0c9f-463a-a710-cacb38cea0a3\n---\n\n**Shadow Frontier** at `/home/john/mynotes/shadow_frontier/` (in the syracuse-confinement repo; pushed 2026-06-10, commit 9a74c80). Successor to [[project-defect-cocycle-csuite]] per `deterministic_equidistribution_theory/critiques/dc_next_steps.md`.\n\n**Mission:** the surviving Collatz counterexample class after the Finite Spectral Shadows program = high-complexity, calibrated (mean → log₂3), non-coboundary phase-biased, mixed-(2,3)-adically coherent ghost resisting every finite max-plus certificate. Three targets:\n1. **Banded S-unit rigidity** (Target 1): many block identities 2^B x′ − 3^p x = A in a band ⟹ exponent vectors (B_{i,j}, p−1−j) collapse to finitely many linear patterns (ESS/subspace) = repeated/periodic blocks = dead. Diagnostic: Z-rank of exponent-vector differences in high-deviation vs ordinary windows.\n2. **Band-crossing certificate** (Target 2): no-long-banded-windows escape ⟹ fast band crossing ⟹ b=1-density > ½+δ ⟹ 2-adic near-ghost (x ≡ −1 mod 2^{f(δ)m}) vs positivity. Quantify the all-ones exclusion.\n3. **Mixed-tower certificate enumeration** (Target 3): Karp max-plus over 2^a3^b for symbolic candidates.\n\n**Tooling:** `search/frontier.py` — candidate gen (letter law {1,2,4} with mean=log₂3 + prescribed ord-3 bias), calibration, complexity, 2-adic realizability (ghost test from the predecessor's sturmian_ghost machinery), mixed-tower traps + Karp, expvec rank.\n\n**Pilot 001:** 120/120 calibrated biased high-complexity candidates = ghosts (full-bit-length least reps, no stabilization); none positive-realizable. Q3 (PROGRAM.md): entropy-vs-bias tension — max-entropy law subject to biased marginal is Markov; does its complexity meet the repetition-rigidity threshold in windows?\n\nAIPM initialized (ailog validate ✓). Final dichotomy: long banded windows ⟹ S-unit rigidity; none ⟹ band-crossing certificate.\n","filePath":"/home/john/.claude/projects/-home-john-mynotes/memory/project_shadow_frontier.md","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[],"type":"create","userModified":false}